        skos:definition        "{\"node\": {\n    \"platformclass\": \"vessel of opportunity\",\n    \"notes\": \"Government owned trawler support vessel operating 1974-1980. Served as mothership for fleet involved in the cod war during the 1970's.  Fate unknown.  Built in 1942 as a 4 masted motor schooner called Albatross (cargo-carrying, sail-training ship). In 1967 converted to cargo vessel 'Donna', 1969, sold and became 'Dorothea', sold to the British Government in 1970 and renamed Miranda.\",\n    \"previous_name\": \"Albatross (1942), Donna (1967), Dorothea (1969)\",\n    \"title\": \"MV\",\n    \"commissioned\": 1970\n}}"@en;
